<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma Yin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">853–930</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ma Yin was the founder of Ma Chu, one of the Ten Kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. A carpenter turned soldier from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuzhou">Xuzhou</a>, he came to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunan">Hunan</a> with a band of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> and became master of the region from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changsha">Changsha</a> in 896. Ruling under titles granted by the northern dynasties, he enriched his state through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> trade with northern China.</p></div>
